{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"encrypted communication channel encrypted communication channel","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md","fileName":"Encrypted Communication Channel.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Encrypted Communication Channel","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-09 00:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience]] [[Applied Cryptography and PKI]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Applied Cryptography and PKI","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"encrypted communication channel encrypted communication channel","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md","fileName":"Encrypted Communication Channel.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Encrypted Communication Channel","heading":"Encrypted Communication Channel","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An encrypted communication channel protects data moving between endpoints from being read or altered easily in transit. The peers establish cryptographic parameters and keys, commonly using an identity certificate to help start a trusted exchange.\n\nChannel encryption protects the route between the participating endpoints. An application may additionally encrypt the data itself when protection must persist after the channel ends or across intermediate systems.\n\nThe source describes SSL/TLS session establishment as a client-server exchange in which a certificate is presented and authenticated, supported cipher suites are compared, and keys are exchanged. The established channel combines asymmetric key management with efficient symmetric protection for transmitted data.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Applied Cryptography and PKI","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"encrypted communication channel encrypted communication channel","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Encrypted Communication Channel.md","fileName":"Encrypted Communication Channel.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Encrypted Communication Channel","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cloudcomputing_mit.epub]]\n\n[[cybersecurity.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Applied Cryptography and PKI","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}